findings.what:
The builder still has to decide three things:
- which route to take;
- how a route-W agent that 'stops' at each step's end goes on to the next step (a workflow or Agent-tool agent cannot pause and resume);
- when the main session runs the insert script's part 1 and part 3 in the worktree, relative to the agent's check.mjs runs. If part 1 is not in place before step 1's check.mjs, contract r2 fails.
The brief's own bar is that a builder can follow it without deciding anything.

